                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Really solid continuation of the series after playing all Raziel-centric games.\r\n\r\nTimeline in the overall franchise is a mess, but this game still carries enough continuity and contains familiar faces to appreciate. For how rudimentary the controls, combat, and level design are, they are surprisingly engaging. Controls suffer a bit from modern hardware (I used a DualSense controller), but once you get used to it, the game plays very smoothly. The combat is fun and requires some strategising instead of just slashing away at your enemies. Level design is decent and offers a unique feel to each area, especially in the late-game sections compared to the early-game. Levels contained fun but basic puzzles, challenging enemies, and great ambiance.\r\n\r\nThe voice acting is once again phenomenal and really help bring the characters to life. Although not as complex as the Raziel-centric games in the series, the plot is intriguing enough to keep me wanting to explore more. The powerups you unlock felt purposeful and were well integrated in solving puzzles to traverse a certain area. \"Hidden\" chests did not feel so hidden though, with most of them in plain sight. Music design was very nice too with that distinct LoK feeling. Sound effects suffer a bit from the limited hardware in the time with overly loud sounds playing on repeat in certain areas.\r\n\r\nOverall a solid game that holds up really well to todays standard. Highly recommend if you are a fan of the series.",
